In MATLAB, you can use the `patch` function to create a 3D surface. Here is an example code to plot the cone of positive definite matrices:

```matlab
x = 0:0.1:10;
z = 0:0.1:10;
Y1 = sqrt(x .* z);
Y2 = -sqrt(x .* z);

figure;
patch(x, Y1, z, 'FaceColor', 'blue', 'EdgeColor', 'none');
patch(x, Y2, z, 'FaceColor', 'blue', 'EdgeColor', 'none');
view(3);
axis equal;
title('Cone of Positive Definite Matrices');
xlabel('x');
ylabel('y');
zlabel('z');
```

